OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789686235
OL,1,Wpp0                               G7/20
OL,2,Wj5{5jj5s1FPAISLEY HAS 'FRANK'
OL,3,W/*%/,$/..%,.%FMEETING WITH TRIMBLE
OL,4,G`````````````
OL,5,FThe new Ulster Unionist Party leader,
OL,6,FDavid Trimble, had his first meeting
OL,7,Ftoday with DUP leader Ian Paisley.
OL,8,F
OL,9,GAfterwards both men agreed that their
OL,10, talks - at Dr Paisley's home - had been
OL,11, frank but friendly, although the Ulster
OL,12, Unionist leader would not commit
OL,13, himself to a voting pact at Westminster
OL,15, Mr Trimble is to see John Major
OL,16, tomorrow and said he would soon be
OL,17, arranging meetings with John Bruton and
OL,18, party leaders in the Republic.
OL,20, Earlier, the DUP leader dismissed the
OL,21, establishment of a single Unionist
OL,22, party as proposed by David Trimble.
OL,23,V]DFrom 18-09-95   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11808
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789686235
OL,1,Wpp0                               G8/20
OL,2,Wj5{5jj5s1FIRA PRISONER
OL,3,W/*%/,$/..%,.%FTRANSFERED TO NI
OL,4,G`````````````
OL,5,FOne of the longest serving IRA
OL,6,Fprisoners has been transferred from
OL,7,Fjail in Britain to Maghaberry prison
OL,8,Foutside Lisburn.
OL,9,F
OL,10, Paul Norney has served 20 years of a
OL,11, life sentence for terrorist offences,
OL,12, and had been in the top security
OL,13, Whitemoor prison on the Isle of Wight.
OL,15, Over 20 prisoners have now been
OL,16, transferred to jails in the North.
OL,18, There are 27 inmates from the North and
OL,19, the Republic still in jails in Britain.
OL,22,F```````````````````````````````````````
OL,23,V]DFrom 18-09-95   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11809
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789686235
OL,1,Wpp0                               G9/20
OL,2,Wj5{5jj5s1FTRANSFER NOT A SHIFT
OL,3,W/*%/,$/..%,.%FIN UK GOVT POLICY
OL,4,G`````````````
OL,5,FThe North's Security Minister Sir John
OL,6,FWheeler said that the transfer of Paul
OL,7,FNorney did not represent a shift in
OL,8,FBritish government policy.
OL,9,F
OL,10, He said he was always willing to
OL,11, receive prisoners from other
OL,12, jurisdictions but it is always a matter
OL,13, for the sending jurisdiction to decide
OL,14, who should go and when they should go.
OL,16, Sir John also told local councillors
OL,17, that the decision whether or not to
OL,18, dismantle the controversial Rosemount
OL,19, watch tower in Derry was not his.
OL,21, He said the decision to remove the
OL,22, tower lay with the RUC Chief
OL,23, Constable & the GOC of the British Army
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11810
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789686235
OL,1,Wpp0                              G10/20
OL,2,Wj5{5jj5s1FGOVT TO MEET
OL,3,W/*%/,$/..%,.%FUDP LEADERS TOMORROW
OL,4,G`````````````
OL,5,FThe Government will meet leaders of the
OL,6,FUlster Democratic Party in Dublin
OL,7,Ftomorrow afternoon.
OL,8,F
OL,9, A meeting with the Progressive Unionist
OL,10, Party is scheduled for Wednesday.
OL,12, These are the first formal meetings
OL,13, between the Government and the fringe
OL,14, loyalist parties.
OL,16, A spokesman said they are part of the
OL,17, continuing bi-lateral meetings the Govt
OL,18, has been having with parties in the
OL,19, North to review the peace process.
OL,23,V]DFrom 18-09-95   teletextarchive.com
